   "source": [
    "📄 PDF Text Extraction Pipeline (Digital + Image-Based)\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook extracts text from PDF files using two methods:\n",
    "\n",
    "    PyMuPDF: For digital (searchable) PDFs, offering fast and direct text extraction.\n",
    "\n",
    "    TrOCR (by Microsoft): For scanned/image-based PDFs using a vision-language transformer model.\n",
    "\n",
    "🔧 Setup Steps:\n",
    "\n",
    "    Install required libraries: transformers, torch, PyMuPDF, pillow.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Load all PDF files from the /content/pdf folder.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Attempt to extract text with PyMuPDF. If that fails (e.g., for image-based content), fallback to TrOCR for OCR-based extraction.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Save the extracted text to /content/output, with a preview of each result in the console.\n",
    "\n",
    "This approach ensures robust extraction from both digital and scanned PDFs using state-of-the-art NLP/vision tools."
