   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "source": [
    "🤖 Anomaly Detection & Classification of High-Severity Wazuh Logs\n",
    "\n",
    "This section applies machine learning to identify and retain meaningful high-severity logs (rule.level >= 7) using an unsupervised anomaly detection approach.\n",
    "🔬 What it does:\n",
    "\n",
    "    📥 Load and Filter Logs\n",
    "\n",
    "        Loads the cleaned dataset (ahmed.csv)\n",
    "\n",
    "        Focuses only on logs with high severity: rule.level >= 7\n",
    "\n",
    "    🔧 Feature Engineering with Text and Numeric Data\n",
    "\n",
    "        Uses StandardScaler for rule.level\n",
    "\n",
    "        Uses TF-IDF Vectorizer for rule.description and full_log (max 1000 features each)\n",
    "\n",
    "    🌲 Anomaly Detection Model\n",
    "\n",
    "        Builds a pipeline with IsolationForest (unsupervised anomaly detection)\n",
    "\n",
    "        Flags logs as either \"good\" (1) or \"bad\" (0) based on anomaly score\n",
    "\n",
    "    📤 Export Results\n",
    "\n",
    "        wazuh_logs_good.csv: Only the logs flagged as \"good\"\n",
    "\n",
    "        wazuh_logs_classified.csv: All high-severity logs with a new column is_good\n",
    "\n",
    "    📊 Visual Insights\n",
    "\n",
    "        Bar chart: Good vs. Bad log counts (saved as classification_distribution.png)\n",
    "\n",
    "        Rule level breakdown by classification\n",
    "\n",
    "        Top 5 most frequent rule descriptions in good logs\n",
    "\n",
    "    📄 Summary Table\n",
    "\n",
    "        Shows the number of good and bad logs\n",
    "\n",
    "        Describes what each CSV file contains\n",
    "\n",
    "This ML-based filter ensures that only relevant, clean, and non-noisy critical logs are passed downstream for further summarization or reporting."
   ],
   "metadata": {
    "id": "zi4FD0ZXd-2m"
   }
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "from sklearn.feature_extraction.text import TfidfVectorizer\n",
    "from sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\n",
    "from sklearn.ensemble import IsolationForest\n",
    "from sklearn.pipeline import make_pipeline\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load the CSV file\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv('ahmed.csv')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Filter logs with rule.level >= 7\n",
    "df_clean = df[df['rule.level'] >= 7].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Prepare features\n",
    "X = df_clean[['rule.level', 'rule.description', 'full_log']]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Define preprocessor\n",
    "preprocessor = ColumnTransformer(\n",
    "    transformers=[\n",
    "        ('level', StandardScaler(), ['rule.level']),\n",
    "        ('description', TfidfVectorizer(max_features=1000, stop_words='english'), 'rule.description'),\n",
    "        ('full_log', TfidfVectorizer(max_features=1000, stop_words='english'), 'full_log')\n",
    "    ])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create pipeline with Isolation Forest\n",
    "model = make_pipeline(\n",
    "    preprocessor,\n",
    "    IsolationForest(contamination=0.1, random_state=42)\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Fit and predict (Isolation Forest assigns -1 for anomalies (bad) and 1 for inliers (good))\n",
    "df_clean['is_good'] = model.fit_predict(X)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Convert predictions to binary (1 for good, 0 for bad)\n",
    "df_clean['is_good'] = df_clean['is_good'].apply(lambda x: 1 if x == 1 else 0)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Filter good logs\n",
    "df_good = df_clean[df_clean['is_good'] == 1].copy()\n",
    "df_good.to_csv('wazuh_logs_good.csv', index=False)\n",
    "print(\"✅ Saved good logs to 'wazuh_logs_good.csv'\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Save full classified DataFrame\n",
    "df_clean.to_csv('wazuh_logs_classified.csv', index=False)\n",
    "print(\"✅ Saved classified DataFrame to 'wazuh_logs_classified.csv'\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Summary\n",
    "good_count = df_clean['is_good'].sum()\n",
    "print(f\"\\n📊 Classification Results:\")\n",
    "print(f\"Good Logs: {good_count}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Bad Logs: {len(df_clean) - good_count}\")"
   ],
   "metadata": {
