    "Executive Summary (200-300 words):\n",
    "\n",
    "Summarize key findings (e.g., detection gaps, compliance issues), strengths (e.g., log collection), and weaknesses (e.g., manual response).\n",
    "\n",
    "Highlight 2-3 high-priority recommendations (e.g., automate incident response, achieve NIST 800-53 compliance).\n",
    "\n",
    "Emphasize banking regulatory context (e.g., GDPR, PCI-DSS).\n",
    "Introduction (150-200 words):\n",
    "State the audit’s purpose and scope (SOC operations, log analysis, compliance).\n",
    "Describe the methodology (e.g., log review, NIST 800-53, C2M2 Level 3 assessment).\n",
    "Note banking-specific regulatory requirements (e.g., FFIEC, GDPR).\n",
    "\n",
    "Analysis:\n",
    "3.1. Log Analysis (150-200 words):\n",
    "Detail specific events (e.g., failed password attempts from external IPs), risks (e.g., brute-force attacks), and detection gaps.\n",
    "\n",
    "Reference NIST 800-53 controls (e.g., AC-7, SI-4) and assess implications for banking security.\n",
    "\n",
    "3.2. SOC Operations (150-200 words):\n",
    "\n",
    "Evaluate workflows, tools (e.g., Wazuh, TheHive), detection (e.g., behavioral analytics), and automation.\n",
    "\n",
    "Highlight strengths (e.g., real-time monitoring) and weaknesses (e.g., manual escalation).\n",
    "\n",
    "Compliance Assessment (150-200 words):\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Assess compliance with NIST 800-53, GDPR, and PCI-DSS based on input (e.g., weak password policies, unauthorized access).\n",
    "\n",
    "Identify gaps (e.g., missing audit logs) and propose remediation (e.g., enforce MFA, conduct configuration audits).\n",
    "\n",
    "Maturity Assessment (150-200 words):\n",
    "\n",
    "Rate SOC maturity using C2M2 (e.g., Level 3, Reactive) with justification (e.g., manual protocols, limited automation).\n",
    "\n",
    "Recommendations (150-200 words):\n",
    "\n",
    "Provide 6-8 prioritized, actionable recommendations (e.g., deploy automated response with Shuffle, align with NIST 800-53 AC-7, enhance logging).\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Align with banking standards and C2M2.\n",
    "\n",
    "Conclusion (150-200 words):\n",
    "\n",
    "Summarize audit value, key actions, and next steps for SOC improvement.\n",
    "\n",
    "Reinforce banking security needs.\n",
    "\n",
    "Requirements:\n",
    "\n",
    "Use professional, banking-industry tone and terminology.\n",
    "\n",
    "Structure with numbered sections (e.g., 1., 2., 3.1., 3.2.).\n",
    "\n",
    "Explicitly reference input data (e.g., ‘failed password attempts,’ ‘root access violations’).\n",
    "\n",
    "Ensure recommendations are specific, prioritized, and tied to NIST 800-53 and C2M2.\n",
    "\n",
    "Produce 1200-1500 words, ensuring no section is truncated.\n",
    "\n",
    "If input lacks details, infer reasonable banking SOC specifics (e.g., assume manual workflows need SOAR automation).\n",
    "\n",
    "Format as plain text for .txt file saving.\n",
    "\n",
    "Avoid generic content; focus on input-driven analysis and banking context.\n",
    "\n",
    "Output: Return the full audit report as a plain text string, ensuring all sections are complete and meet the word count.\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Initialize Gemini model\n",
    "model = genai.GenerativeModel(\"gemini-1.5-flash\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Send the prompt to Gemini with retry logic\n",
    "max_retries = 3\n",
    "for attempt in range(max_retries):\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        response = model.generate_content(\n",
    "            prompt,\n",
    "            generation_config={\n",
    "                \"max_output_tokens\": 8000,  # Supports 1200-1500 words\n",
    "                \"temperature\": 0.6,  # Precise, professional tone\n",
    "                \"top_p\": 1\n",
    "            }\n",
    "        )\n",
    "        full_report = response.text.strip()\n",
    "        break\n",
    "    except Exception as e:\n",
    "        error_message = f\"Attempt {attempt + 1}/{max_retries} - Error calling Gemini API: {str(e)}\"\n",
    "        print(error_message)\n",
    "        if attempt < max_retries - 1:\n",
    "            print(\"Retrying in 6 seconds to avoid overloading the model...\")\n",
    "            time.sleep(6)  # Respect rate limits\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            print(\"\\nAll retries failed. Check your Gemini API key and quota at https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey\")\n",
    "            print(\"Consider using the local model (Lily-Cybersecurity-7B) as a fallback.\")\n",
    "            full_report = f\"Failed to generate audit report: {error_message}\"\n",
    "            break\n",
    "\n",
    "# Save the full audit report to a file\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    with open(OUTPUT_FILE, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n",
    "        f.write(\"=== Full Audit Report ===\\n\")\n",
    "        f.write(full_report)\n",
    "        f.write(\"\\n\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Full audit report saved to {OUTPUT_FILE}\")\n",
    "except Exception as e:\n",
    "    print(f\"Error saving report to {OUTPUT_FILE}: {str(e)}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Optional: Display the contents of the saved file for verification\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    with open(OUTPUT_FILE, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n",
    "        print(\"\\nContents of full_audit_report.txt:\")\n",
    "        print(f.read())\n",
    "except Exception as e:\n",
    "    print(f\"Error reading {OUTPUT_FILE}: {str(e)}\")"
